					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1166893#post-2301350</guid>
				<title>Re: I don&#039;t understand!</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1166893/maybe-god-will-forgive-you-if-we-both-beg#post-2301350</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 23 May 2015 01:40:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Thekillerax</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1832151</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I don't see where you'd be having trouble. In an alternate universe somewhere, several events occurred that made the Foundation less strict than they typically are, and so they allowed <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-073">Cain</a> to try to reason with <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-076">Able</a>, his brother. Most of the stuff they're talking about comes from the Bible, since, in biblical lore, Cain and Able were the sons of Adam and Eve, with Cain growing jealous of Able and killing him, making him the world's first murderer. God was disappointed but showed he still loved Cain by giving him a mark that caused any damage done to him to be reflected back at the attacker. The SCP twist is that Cain has come to regret his actions while Able grew resentful and possibly got involved with the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-140">Daevites</a>, leading to his ability to respawn indefinitely. In this tale, the two forgive each other and finally move on.<br /> I'm assuming you're not that familiarized with the SCP lore, in which case you should definitely read some of the older works. They may not be the best in terms of quality, but they're frequently referenced, so it'd do you good to read up on those before delving into tales like these.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
